1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,700
[Disclaimer:
All depicted events are fictional

2
00:00:01,730 --> 00:00:03,440
and for entertainment purposes only;
viewer discretion is advised]

3
00:00:12,080 --> 00:00:17,360
[Your Third Series]

4
00:00:17,920 --> 00:00:18,970
I...

5
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:20,920
want you to bring Mr. Sarm back to us.

6
00:00:23,040 --> 00:00:25,040
All I have to do is bring Mr. Sarm back

7
00:00:25,410 --> 00:00:27,720
How hard can it be?

8
00:00:28,710 --> 00:00:29,560
Sarm!

9
00:00:29,600 --> 00:00:30,770
It's his first heartbreak,

10
00:00:30,800 --> 00:00:31,820
so it hurts a fair bit.

11
00:00:31,860 --> 00:00:34,290
Based on my twin sense,

12
00:00:34,320 --> 00:00:36,720
I'm guessing that he's probably
taking some time off on some beach.

13
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:38,600
An island in the South...

14
00:00:38,860 --> 00:00:41,560
Can you pick one for me?

15
00:00:42,320 --> 00:00:43,760
Ko Pha-ngan.

16
00:00:45,230 --> 00:00:46,880
But danger awaits.

17
00:00:47,050 --> 00:00:48,460
You are fated to suffer

18
00:00:48,490 --> 00:00:49,880
the same misfortune as your parents:

19
00:00:49,960 --> 00:00:51,280
either by falling into the water

20
00:00:51,320 --> 00:00:52,640
or by drowning.

21
00:00:53,900 --> 00:00:55,700
You have been given
an impossible task, correct?

22
00:00:55,740 --> 00:00:56,840
Do you think we're friends?

23
00:00:57,000 --> 00:00:58,280
You're all bark and no bite.

24
00:00:58,310 --> 00:00:58,860
Do you think prey

25
00:00:58,890 --> 00:01:00,840
can escape the claws of this mighty tiger?

26
00:01:03,170 --> 00:01:04,349
It seems like a lot of people

27
00:01:04,370 --> 00:01:06,350
have been looking
for you lately.

28
00:01:06,380 --> 00:01:07,260
Then who?

29
00:01:08,460 --> 00:01:09,370
It's whatever, then.

30
00:01:09,960 --> 00:01:11,270
I don't really care anyway.

31
00:01:12,120 --> 00:01:12,810
I'll be going now.

32
00:01:32,300 --> 00:01:33,000
Mr. Sib?!

33
00:01:37,960 --> 00:01:38,660
Yes,

34
00:01:38,970 --> 00:01:39,680
Mr. Sib.

35
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:41,320
You're still not awake?

36
00:01:41,630 --> 00:01:42,600
I am now.

37
00:01:43,070 --> 00:01:44,670
Is there a problem, Mr. Sib?

38
00:01:44,810 --> 00:01:45,960
Any news?

39
00:01:46,500 --> 00:01:48,259
I have found Mr. Sarm.

40
00:01:48,300 --> 00:01:49,120
Where is he?

41
00:01:49,210 --> 00:01:50,560
On Ko Pha-ngan.

42
00:01:51,070 --> 00:01:52,759
I ran into him at a restaurant.

43
00:01:52,850 --> 00:01:53,770
But at the moment,

44
00:01:53,850 --> 00:01:56,259
I still do not know exactly
where he is staying.

45
00:01:56,720 --> 00:01:58,220
I believe he is at a bungalow

46
00:01:58,250 --> 00:01:59,400
near Haad Rin.

47
00:01:59,770 --> 00:02:01,060
If not,

48
00:02:01,620 --> 00:02:03,550
he is probably somewhere around that area.

49
00:02:03,760 --> 00:02:04,760
Does this mean...

50
00:02:04,850 --> 00:02:06,600
you're still on the island?

51
00:02:07,120 --> 00:02:08,050
Precisely.

52
00:02:08,220 --> 00:02:09,009
Good.

53
00:02:09,180 --> 00:02:10,320
You've made good progress.

54
00:02:10,600 --> 00:02:12,100
No wonder

55
00:02:12,160 --> 00:02:14,000
you were able to track him down

56
00:02:14,160 --> 00:02:15,160
in just a few days.

57
00:02:16,280 --> 00:02:17,320
Well done.

58
00:02:18,060 --> 00:02:19,960
Impressive. You live up to your name.

59
00:02:29,410 --> 00:02:30,760
It's time to end this mission

60
00:02:30,790 --> 00:02:33,370
by bringing the teeny-tiny tiger home.

61
00:02:38,440 --> 00:02:43,120
[Your Third Series]

62
00:02:52,890 --> 00:02:56,820
♫Still feeling lonely? Well, you've got me,♫

63
00:02:56,850 --> 00:03:01,290
♫Keeping you busy every day♫

64
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:05,940
♫I might not be the one you wanted,♫

65
00:03:06,010 --> 00:03:10,710
♫But give it time, you'll love me anyway♫

66
00:03:11,160 --> 00:03:15,640
♫It's your heart, so it's your choice,♫

67
00:03:15,690 --> 00:03:20,130
♫I won't ever stand in your way♫

68
00:03:20,270 --> 00:03:24,530
♫But when they make you blue,♫

69
00:03:24,570 --> 00:03:28,220
♫Can you please let me take care of you?♫

70
00:03:29,250 --> 00:03:33,920
♫I'm here to love you as myself,
not as a surrogate♫

71
00:03:33,960 --> 00:03:37,710
♫Let me be your safe space
when you need a break♫

72
00:03:37,740 --> 00:03:42,730
♫Who cares if I'm not your first or second?♫

73
00:03:42,840 --> 00:03:47,610
♫At least being your third still counts♫

74
00:03:47,640 --> 00:03:52,230
♫I'm here to love you,
no matter who left you with heartache♫

75
00:03:52,280 --> 00:03:55,940
♫Just let me heal your heart,
lending you my aid♫

76
00:03:55,970 --> 00:04:01,080
♫Have faith and believe in love once more♫

77
00:04:01,110 --> 00:04:03,090
♫'Cause good love is your Lucky Third♫

78
00:04:03,120 --> 00:04:06,320
♫Your Third, can it be me, love?♫

79
00:04:06,360 --> 00:04:09,680
[Your Third Series]

80
00:04:25,430 --> 00:04:26,270
There he is.

81
00:04:26,310 --> 00:04:27,580
I have found him.

82
00:04:27,620 --> 00:04:28,640
Should I approach him directly,

83
00:04:28,670 --> 00:04:30,480
or call the insurance company first

84
00:04:30,510 --> 00:04:32,600
in case he gets feisty again?

85
00:04:39,290 --> 00:04:40,290
Hello...

86
00:04:45,240 --> 00:04:46,780
I mean no harm.

87
00:04:48,780 --> 00:04:50,880
Mr. Sarm, do you...

88
00:04:51,080 --> 00:04:52,510
have a moment?

89
00:04:53,980 --> 00:04:54,780
I don't.

90
00:04:56,460 --> 00:04:57,159
Occupied by loneliness.

91
00:04:59,480 --> 00:05:00,710
If that is the case,

92
00:05:01,930 --> 00:05:03,660
could you spare me

93
00:05:03,690 --> 00:05:05,640
- five minutes?
- Not even a second.

94
00:05:06,980 --> 00:05:08,560
And stop bugging me already.

95
00:05:08,590 --> 00:05:09,120
Go away

96
00:05:09,160 --> 00:05:10,840
before I lose any more of my patience.

97
00:05:13,910 --> 00:05:14,850
Remember, Jam:

98
00:05:14,880 --> 00:05:15,970
"No trouble.

99
00:05:16,000 --> 00:05:17,700
Just bring him home."

100
00:05:17,880 --> 00:05:18,770
"No trouble.

101
00:05:18,810 --> 00:05:20,040
With that being said,

102
00:05:23,880 --> 00:05:25,070
"No trouble.

103
00:05:25,130 --> 00:05:26,560
Just bring him home."

104
00:05:30,880 --> 00:05:31,850
"No trouble.

105
00:05:31,880 --> 00:05:33,110
Just bring him home..."

106
00:05:35,159 --> 00:05:36,159
Still sticking around?

107
00:05:37,580 --> 00:05:39,480
I've got an idea.
If you don't leave right now,

108
00:05:39,510 --> 00:05:41,850
I'll call a shaman
and seal your soul in a pot

109
00:05:42,080 --> 00:05:43,180
so you'll disappear.

110
00:05:43,480 --> 00:05:43,970
Or...

111
00:05:44,010 --> 00:05:45,159
How about this pot of tom yum?

112
00:05:45,200 --> 00:05:45,980
"Cause trouble..."

113
00:05:46,010 --> 00:05:46,830
Cause trouble.

114
00:05:46,860 --> 00:05:47,770
Cause trouble!

115
00:05:47,810 --> 00:05:49,200
Don't bring him home!

116
00:05:49,390 --> 00:05:51,080
No matter how many times
you tell me to leave,

117
00:05:51,280 --> 00:05:52,920
I must tell you the truth, Mr. Sarm.

118
00:05:52,960 --> 00:05:53,650
Right now,

119
00:05:53,680 --> 00:05:55,370
it has been six months
since you disappeared.

120
00:05:56,180 --> 00:05:59,200
This means that
you abandoned your work for six months.

121
00:05:59,450 --> 00:06:01,600
Adisuan Farm is in trouble, you see.

122
00:06:02,560 --> 00:06:03,490
Adisuan Farm?

123
00:06:04,410 --> 00:06:06,700
And based on
what I have investigated so far,

124
00:06:07,680 --> 00:06:10,760
there are still many things
that I have not been able to verify yet.

125
00:06:12,130 --> 00:06:14,200
You should hurry back and deal with them.

126
00:06:16,510 --> 00:06:17,510
With that being said,

127
00:06:18,550 --> 00:06:19,990
please return home, Mr. Sarm.

128
00:06:21,540 --> 00:06:23,410
Everyone needs you.

129
00:06:35,310 --> 00:06:36,680
How could there be any problems?

130
00:06:36,850 --> 00:06:38,340
I've already put everything in place.

131
00:06:38,370 --> 00:06:40,770
There's no way anything could go wrong.

132
00:06:40,800 --> 00:06:41,800
100 percent!

133
00:06:42,020 --> 00:06:42,810
Understand,

134
00:06:42,840 --> 00:06:43,900
Snoop?

135
00:06:44,310 --> 00:06:45,320
Gosh...

136
00:06:45,370 --> 00:06:46,800
You're tricking me with that?

137
00:06:46,850 --> 00:06:47,590
Oh...

138
00:06:47,810 --> 00:06:48,470
You know,

139
00:06:48,600 --> 00:06:49,680
only an idiot

140
00:06:49,730 --> 00:06:50,880
would fall for such a stupid trick.

141
00:06:50,970 --> 00:06:51,880
An idiot!

142
00:06:55,430 --> 00:06:56,180
If that is the case...

143
00:06:56,210 --> 00:06:58,610
In case you have not noticed,
Mr. Sarmonkey,

144
00:06:59,400 --> 00:07:02,840
your reputation
among the workers at your farm

145
00:07:02,930 --> 00:07:04,400
is now in shambles.

146
00:07:06,140 --> 00:07:08,480
Everyone is getting frustrated
by the countless projects

147
00:07:08,540 --> 00:07:09,720
you started yourself

148
00:07:09,990 --> 00:07:11,240
but never followed through on.

149
00:07:11,260 --> 00:07:11,810
Is that so?

150
00:07:11,840 --> 00:07:13,040
They have been abandoned.

151
00:07:14,780 --> 00:07:15,680
You mean set adrift on a raft?

152
00:07:17,600 --> 00:07:18,320
Help!

153
00:07:18,470 --> 00:07:19,770
I have been set adrift on a raft!

154
00:07:20,180 --> 00:07:20,780
Goodness me.

155
00:07:20,860 --> 00:07:22,000
What if they got stranded on an island?

156
00:07:22,040 --> 00:07:23,400
"I don't wanna be alone!"

157
00:07:23,430 --> 00:07:24,370
"Aww, I'll drown

158
00:07:24,400 --> 00:07:25,600
- Above all,
- or be stranded."

159
00:07:25,650 --> 00:07:27,560
your family is deeply worried.

160
00:07:30,820 --> 00:07:32,300
It would be best if you returned.

161
00:07:40,510 --> 00:07:41,560
First and foremost,

162
00:07:43,020 --> 00:07:44,120
my name is Sarm!

163
00:07:44,310 --> 00:07:45,280
Not "Sarmonkey!"

164
00:07:45,590 --> 00:07:46,120
My name...

165
00:07:46,150 --> 00:07:46,710
isn't...

166
00:07:46,740 --> 00:07:47,970
Sarmonkey.

167
00:07:48,200 --> 00:07:48,780
I'm not a monkey!

168
00:07:48,820 --> 00:07:50,390
The same goes for me.
My name is Jam,

169
00:07:50,420 --> 00:07:52,190
not "Snoop" like you have been calling me.

170
00:07:53,480 --> 00:07:55,170
I am not finished yet.

171
00:07:57,180 --> 00:07:58,480
In two weeks,

172
00:07:58,920 --> 00:08:00,240
Ms. Namnueng is getting married.

173
00:08:01,290 --> 00:08:03,400
She wants you to be there
on her special day.

174
00:08:03,500 --> 00:08:05,040
Oh, God!

175
00:08:05,210 --> 00:08:05,920
Woo!

176
00:08:09,050 --> 00:08:10,660
First, you used Adisuan Farm.

177
00:08:10,950 --> 00:08:12,240
Now you're using Namnueng?

178
00:08:12,610 --> 00:08:13,720
Let me tell you something.

179
00:08:14,230 --> 00:08:15,190
She doesn't like it!

180
00:08:15,230 --> 00:08:16,440
She doesn't care about love!

181
00:08:16,780 --> 00:08:18,600
Someone like her will never get married.

182
00:08:18,650 --> 00:08:20,520
And yet, Mr. Sib got married.

183
00:08:38,990 --> 00:08:39,990
You weren't trying to scare me,

184
00:08:40,190 --> 00:08:40,960
were you?

185
00:08:45,430 --> 00:08:47,000
Why would I do such a thing?

186
00:08:47,570 --> 00:08:50,080
I am not a ghost, like you called me.

187
00:08:50,800 --> 00:08:52,490
How could I possibly scare you?

188
00:08:54,500 --> 00:08:55,500
So...

189
00:08:56,940 --> 00:08:57,790
shall we return home?

190
00:09:03,350 --> 00:09:04,080
I'm not returning.

191
00:09:06,380 --> 00:09:08,080
And stop forcing me already.

192
00:09:10,100 --> 00:09:11,890
If you are not coming home today,

193
00:09:12,580 --> 00:09:13,760
then when are you going to?

194
00:09:14,590 --> 00:09:15,480
And what's it to you?

195
00:09:15,510 --> 00:09:17,120
If you do, my mission will be complete.

196
00:09:17,260 --> 00:09:17,690
Oh?

197
00:09:17,730 --> 00:09:18,810
Mission complete.

198
00:09:18,860 --> 00:09:19,920
Complete...

199
00:09:21,200 --> 00:09:23,170
Please, Mr. Sarm.

200
00:09:23,800 --> 00:09:25,580
Please come home with me.

201
00:09:26,350 --> 00:09:27,160
If there is anything you need,

202
00:09:27,200 --> 00:09:28,770
please let me...

203
00:09:32,070 --> 00:09:32,580
Hey!

204
00:09:32,680 --> 00:09:33,040
Hey!

205
00:09:33,080 --> 00:09:33,890
What the hell is this?!

206
00:09:33,980 --> 00:09:34,580
Hey!

207
00:09:34,620 --> 00:09:35,200
Don't move!

208
00:09:36,290 --> 00:09:37,030
I said don't move!

209
00:09:37,050 --> 00:09:38,360
Or I'm going to stab him!

210
00:09:38,730 --> 00:09:39,580
Do it!

211
00:09:40,230 --> 00:09:42,000
There are security cameras
all over the beach.

212
00:09:42,270 --> 00:09:44,200
Your names will be known across the island.

213
00:09:44,520 --> 00:09:45,980
If you make it out alive today,

214
00:09:46,720 --> 00:09:48,360
you won't be so lucky next time.

215
00:09:53,410 --> 00:09:54,490
It's damn near impossible...

216
00:09:54,820 --> 00:09:55,880
to track you down,

217
00:09:56,800 --> 00:09:57,660
Mr. Sarm.

218
00:10:03,870 --> 00:10:04,680
- Hey!
- Keep moving!

219
00:10:20,270 --> 00:10:21,090
Why did you stop?!

220
00:10:21,440 --> 00:10:22,040
- Hey!
- Hey!

221
00:10:29,980 --> 00:10:31,080
Woo-hoo!

222
00:10:36,250 --> 00:10:36,760
Come.

223
00:10:42,350 --> 00:10:43,170
Ha-ha!

224
00:10:43,910 --> 00:10:44,390
Let's go!

225
00:10:46,170 --> 00:10:47,100
Mr. Sarm!

226
00:10:47,400 --> 00:10:47,980
Mr. Sarm!!

227
00:10:48,410 --> 00:10:49,240
Mr. Sarm...

228
00:10:52,600 --> 00:10:54,180
- We'll flank them from there!
- Yes.

229
00:10:56,010 --> 00:10:57,480
Quickly! Come on!

230
00:11:22,450 --> 00:11:23,780
Hey! Where are they?!

231
00:11:28,120 --> 00:11:28,860
Hey!

232
00:11:36,980 --> 00:11:37,620
Hey...

233
00:11:38,350 --> 00:11:39,770
From Pak Chong to Ko Pha-ngan,

234
00:11:39,950 --> 00:11:40,990
were you being followed?

235
00:11:43,300 --> 00:11:44,300
I was not.

236
00:11:44,810 --> 00:11:46,040
Who do you think they are?

237
00:11:46,410 --> 00:11:48,040
They were probably not your average thugs.

238
00:11:48,310 --> 00:11:49,900
They were not after our belongings,

239
00:11:50,550 --> 00:11:51,960
but you.

240
00:11:53,880 --> 00:11:55,390
Moreover, they knew your name.

241
00:11:56,210 --> 00:11:58,070
It seems like
they have been looking for you.

242
00:12:01,290 --> 00:12:02,790
Apart from you, who Sib sent here...

243
00:12:03,690 --> 00:12:04,560
did he send anyone else?

244
00:12:05,300 --> 00:12:07,490
He only tasked me with bringing you home.

245
00:12:08,100 --> 00:12:09,280
I know nothing apart from that.

246
00:12:09,520 --> 00:12:10,180
Oh,

247
00:12:10,840 --> 00:12:12,270
perhaps they're your enemies?

248
00:12:12,900 --> 00:12:14,090
Did you step on someone's toes?

249
00:12:14,250 --> 00:12:15,360
Think carefully.

250
00:12:16,580 --> 00:12:18,780
I think you are the one
who should ask yourself

251
00:12:19,410 --> 00:12:21,240
whether or not you have any enemies.

252
00:12:21,290 --> 00:12:22,520
Seriously, you.

253
00:12:22,560 --> 00:12:23,370
I was at peace,

254
00:12:23,390 --> 00:12:25,080
and here you are causing me trouble.

255
00:12:25,160 --> 00:12:26,280
I'm here to heal my heart,

256
00:12:26,390 --> 00:12:27,920
and here I am
running away from thugs with you.

257
00:12:28,530 --> 00:12:29,760
And where exactly are we going?

258
00:12:29,840 --> 00:12:30,840
To the boat, obviously.

259
00:12:31,110 --> 00:12:32,170
Just as they said.

260
00:12:33,680 --> 00:12:34,680
Are you crazy?!

261
00:12:35,080 --> 00:12:36,440
Why would you walk into their trap?

262
00:12:37,500 --> 00:12:38,580
Never heard of it?

263
00:12:38,890 --> 00:12:41,690
"The safest place
is often the most dangerous one."

264
00:12:52,430 --> 00:12:53,100
What's wrong?

265
00:12:53,290 --> 00:12:55,360
You're as pale as a boiled chicken.

266
00:12:55,920 --> 00:12:56,550
Get up!

267
00:12:56,760 --> 00:12:57,460
Quickly!

268
00:12:57,850 --> 00:12:58,470
Come on!

269
00:12:59,280 --> 00:13:00,290
Get up already.

270
00:13:01,070 --> 00:13:01,960
Make it quick.

271
00:13:08,080 --> 00:13:09,080
Come on!

272
00:13:09,170 --> 00:13:10,490
Can we take it slow, please?

273
00:13:11,370 --> 00:13:12,480
- Where are we going?
- What?!

274
00:13:12,520 --> 00:13:13,260
Hey!

275
00:13:13,300 --> 00:13:14,050
Hey!

276
00:13:14,160 --> 00:13:15,160
My backpack!

277
00:13:15,940 --> 00:13:17,640
Would it kill you
to go without this backpack?

278
00:13:17,680 --> 00:13:18,890
It surely would!

279
00:13:21,780 --> 00:13:22,580
Hey!

280
00:13:23,770 --> 00:13:24,870
Okay, okay.

281
00:13:26,390 --> 00:13:27,780
Then remember this,

282
00:13:28,280 --> 00:13:29,770
and take a good look

283
00:13:30,390 --> 00:13:31,190
at who...

284
00:13:32,470 --> 00:13:33,470
your hero is.

285
00:13:37,780 --> 00:13:38,780
Take a good look

286
00:13:39,480 --> 00:13:41,240
at who your hero is!

287
00:13:45,320 --> 00:13:47,060
Yeah! I got it.

288
00:13:47,920 --> 00:13:49,240
Why did you jump into the water?

289
00:13:49,370 --> 00:13:50,480
You could have just taken it slow.

290
00:13:50,860 --> 00:13:52,280
Normal is boring anyway.

291
00:13:53,160 --> 00:13:54,080
Come on, Snoop!

292
00:13:54,430 --> 00:13:55,160
Help me!

293
00:13:57,540 --> 00:13:58,470
Hold on tight, okay?

294
00:14:01,560 --> 00:14:02,400
Three, two, one!

295
00:14:11,580 --> 00:14:13,000
Oh...

296
00:14:30,160 --> 00:14:31,100
Let's get going already.

297
00:14:31,140 --> 00:14:31,860
We need to hurry.

298
00:14:31,890 --> 00:14:34,400
Why go overboard when we had to hurry?

299
00:14:34,470 --> 00:14:36,200
You picked the worst time to go overboard.

300
00:14:36,240 --> 00:14:36,630
Come on.

301
00:14:36,660 --> 00:14:38,050
You are beyond help.

302
00:14:38,080 --> 00:14:39,560
It is completely soaked!

303
00:14:45,590 --> 00:14:46,290
Uncle.

304
00:14:49,980 --> 00:14:50,980
Does the person you're waiting for

305
00:14:51,010 --> 00:14:51,960
look like this?

306
00:14:52,660 --> 00:14:53,270
Yes.

307
00:14:53,300 --> 00:14:55,640
Make it quick.
I'm dying to eat my wife's cooking.

308
00:14:55,660 --> 00:14:56,240
Okay.

309
00:14:57,520 --> 00:14:58,080
Jam, hop on.

310
00:14:58,150 --> 00:14:58,870
Come on.

311
00:14:59,680 --> 00:15:00,170
Quickly.

312
00:15:00,230 --> 00:15:01,040
But...

313
00:15:01,380 --> 00:15:02,380
No more buts.

314
00:15:02,860 --> 00:15:03,590
Hop on.

315
00:15:07,380 --> 00:15:08,300
Ow...

316
00:15:08,320 --> 00:15:09,200
You!

317
00:15:10,060 --> 00:15:10,630
By the way,

318
00:15:10,660 --> 00:15:12,380
where are you taking us, Uncle?

319
00:15:14,400 --> 00:15:15,480
Where are the other two?

320
00:15:15,600 --> 00:15:16,600
They're not coming.

321
00:15:16,650 --> 00:15:17,370
You see,

322
00:15:17,620 --> 00:15:20,160
this is why
I brought my partner on board instead.

323
00:15:21,000 --> 00:15:22,360
Did you even ask me first?

324
00:15:23,390 --> 00:15:24,070
Jam.

325
00:15:24,640 --> 00:15:25,690
Or are you staying here?

326
00:15:26,650 --> 00:15:27,560
Don't forget

327
00:15:28,230 --> 00:15:30,290
what your mission was

328
00:15:30,600 --> 00:15:31,410
when you came here.

329
00:15:33,860 --> 00:15:34,610
So, Uncle?

330
00:15:34,830 --> 00:15:36,180
The northern beaches of Ko Pha-ngan.

331
00:15:37,260 --> 00:15:37,920
Come on.

332
00:15:40,830 --> 00:15:41,640
Here.

333
00:15:42,900 --> 00:15:43,790
Let's go.

334
00:16:02,720 --> 00:16:03,560
We're almost there.

335
00:16:03,610 --> 00:16:04,610
Over there.

336
00:16:09,400 --> 00:16:10,050
Oh!

337
00:16:12,600 --> 00:16:13,390
Uncle.

338
00:16:13,590 --> 00:16:14,690
Do you even know how to drive?

339
00:16:20,000 --> 00:16:20,720
Oh!

340
00:16:21,520 --> 00:16:22,620
Hey! Jam!

341
00:16:23,200 --> 00:16:23,880
Jam!

342
00:16:24,680 --> 00:16:25,480
Stop the boat!

343
00:16:25,720 --> 00:16:27,080
Uncle! Stop the boat!

344
00:16:27,490 --> 00:16:28,070
Uncle!

345
00:16:28,110 --> 00:16:28,920
Jam!

346
00:16:29,320 --> 00:16:30,320
Jam!

347
00:16:30,680 --> 00:16:32,200
Jam!!

348
00:16:32,230 --> 00:16:33,970
Jam!!

349
00:17:40,280 --> 00:17:41,160
Little Jam...

350
00:17:43,910 --> 00:17:44,760
Jam...

351
00:17:45,170 --> 00:17:45,890
Jam.

352
00:17:46,640 --> 00:17:47,390
Jam.

353
00:17:53,070 --> 00:17:53,970
Little Jam.

354
00:17:54,230 --> 00:17:55,100
Little Jam...

355
00:17:56,300 --> 00:17:57,170
Little Jam.

356
00:18:17,570 --> 00:18:18,190
Jam.

357
00:18:19,050 --> 00:18:19,790
Little Jam.

358
00:18:19,990 --> 00:18:20,480
Little Jam!

359
00:18:34,670 --> 00:18:35,380
Jam.

360
00:18:38,890 --> 00:18:39,690
It's me.

361
00:18:42,380 --> 00:18:43,380
Don't worry.

362
00:18:44,290 --> 00:18:45,290
You're still alive.

363
00:18:52,010 --> 00:18:53,760
Mr. Sarm...

364
00:18:56,040 --> 00:18:57,570
Mr. Sarm...

365
00:18:59,480 --> 00:19:00,600
Don't say it like that.

366
00:19:04,190 --> 00:19:06,220
You're making me nervous.

367
00:20:05,000 --> 00:20:07,160
I was talking to Mr. Sarm this morning

368
00:20:07,360 --> 00:20:08,920
before we were hunted down.

369
00:20:09,530 --> 00:20:12,120
We then had to board a boat
with an inexperienced driver,

370
00:20:12,840 --> 00:20:14,080
and it capsized.

371
00:20:14,920 --> 00:20:17,080
Mr. Sarm carried me to shore.

372
00:20:17,720 --> 00:20:19,320
I got upset with him

373
00:20:19,880 --> 00:20:21,320
before passing out.

374
00:20:21,840 --> 00:20:23,760
So how did I end up here?

375
00:20:27,880 --> 00:20:29,170
- Ta-da!
- Whoa!

376
00:20:29,530 --> 00:20:30,730
You almost died doing your job,

377
00:20:30,780 --> 00:20:31,600
Snoop.

378
00:20:37,910 --> 00:20:38,770
Don't tell me that

379
00:20:39,270 --> 00:20:41,320
you've lost memory,
like they do in soap operas.

380
00:20:47,200 --> 00:20:49,060
Wait! That means that you've forgotten

381
00:20:49,120 --> 00:20:51,100
that I'm Prince Smith

382
00:20:51,160 --> 00:20:52,160
from the House of

383
00:20:52,380 --> 00:20:54,300
Smithru Smithra.

384
00:20:55,260 --> 00:20:55,920
Wow.

385
00:20:59,180 --> 00:21:00,720
And what about the boat driver?

386
00:21:00,830 --> 00:21:01,360
Oh...

387
00:21:01,460 --> 00:21:03,280
The lifeguards came to rescue him
the moment the boat capsized.

388
00:21:03,340 --> 00:21:04,220
As for you,

389
00:21:04,250 --> 00:21:05,500
I jumped into the water

390
00:21:05,530 --> 00:21:07,780
and dove around looking for you...

391
00:21:08,010 --> 00:21:08,800
Then I found you.

392
00:21:09,100 --> 00:21:10,100
I found your backpack, too.

393
00:21:10,140 --> 00:21:11,360
And where is it?

394
00:21:11,390 --> 00:21:12,720
I left it on the fish-drying raft to dry out.

395
00:21:12,820 --> 00:21:13,640
And what about you?

396
00:21:13,810 --> 00:21:15,000
How are you feeling?

397
00:21:23,600 --> 00:21:25,080
I am so hungry,

398
00:21:26,280 --> 00:21:27,880
I am starting to feel dizzy.

399
00:21:28,060 --> 00:21:29,080
If you're okay now,

400
00:21:29,540 --> 00:21:30,400
we'll have some food later.

401
00:21:30,440 --> 00:21:30,960
Oh.

402
00:21:30,980 --> 00:21:31,400
Here.

403
00:21:31,480 --> 00:21:33,000
Ta-da!

404
00:21:33,190 --> 00:21:33,760
Here.

405
00:21:39,180 --> 00:21:40,100
Your outfit.

406
00:21:40,390 --> 00:21:41,510
I've got a new one for you.

407
00:21:41,550 --> 00:21:42,280
What do you think?

408
00:21:42,480 --> 00:21:43,480
Feeling touched yet?

409
00:21:50,210 --> 00:21:52,110
Let me go get changed real quick.

410
00:21:53,690 --> 00:21:54,650
Hey! Ta-da.

411
00:21:54,680 --> 00:21:55,880
Let me lend you a hand.

412
00:22:06,280 --> 00:22:09,060
[Ministry of Public Health]
[Emergency]

413
00:22:09,190 --> 00:22:10,910
What are you going to do now?

414
00:22:11,590 --> 00:22:12,680
I'm going to stay here

415
00:22:13,290 --> 00:22:14,400
for a change of pace.

416
00:22:15,300 --> 00:22:16,300
I've already filmed my MV there.

417
00:22:16,450 --> 00:22:18,080
I used all the landmarks at that beach.

418
00:22:19,190 --> 00:22:20,190
As for you,

419
00:22:20,620 --> 00:22:21,760
it's best if you go home.

420
00:22:22,390 --> 00:22:24,300
You've been getting into trouble
every day here.

421
00:22:24,890 --> 00:22:26,920
You, too, should return home.

422
00:22:36,540 --> 00:22:37,760
It is not yet time.

423
00:22:38,440 --> 00:22:39,280
Let's go.

424
00:22:51,210 --> 00:22:53,190
What about my wallet and phone?

425
00:22:54,590 --> 00:22:55,810
Maybe they were lost at sea.

426
00:22:56,470 --> 00:22:57,880
My phone's gone, too.

427
00:22:57,920 --> 00:22:59,490
This means neither of us...

428
00:22:59,870 --> 00:23:01,080
has any money on us.

429
00:23:01,120 --> 00:23:01,980
Hm...

430
00:23:02,260 --> 00:23:03,110
Only you do.

431
00:23:03,150 --> 00:23:03,920
Not me.

432
00:23:04,220 --> 00:23:05,580
The banknotes got soggy,

433
00:23:05,880 --> 00:23:07,280
but while you were recovering,

434
00:23:07,320 --> 00:23:08,080
I, myself,

435
00:23:08,200 --> 00:23:09,600
went out and withdrew some cash.

436
00:23:10,160 --> 00:23:10,990
And here.

437
00:23:11,420 --> 00:23:12,990
I bought us some yogurt drinks.

438
00:23:13,520 --> 00:23:15,040
I might as well have some.

439
00:23:15,250 --> 00:23:16,240
Ta-da.

440
00:23:22,510 --> 00:23:23,510
Ah! That's refreshing.

441
00:23:23,860 --> 00:23:25,480
Come on, follow your man... Wait!

442
00:23:26,880 --> 00:23:28,440
Can you walk properly?

443
00:23:29,700 --> 00:23:31,310
Here to retrieve the backpack?

444
00:23:31,770 --> 00:23:32,470
Oh.

445
00:23:32,910 --> 00:23:33,760
Thank you.

446
00:23:34,590 --> 00:23:35,430
My backpack.

447
00:23:35,470 --> 00:23:36,190
Mm.

448
00:23:46,740 --> 00:23:47,680
Can you see me clearly now?

449
00:23:48,320 --> 00:23:49,240
Am I still as handsome as ever?

450
00:23:52,340 --> 00:23:53,550
Did Sattawat

451
00:23:53,740 --> 00:23:54,840
send you here

452
00:23:54,920 --> 00:23:56,280
just to bring me home,

453
00:23:56,730 --> 00:23:58,040
or to be my burden?

454
00:23:58,260 --> 00:23:59,860
I could not see very well.

455
00:24:00,770 --> 00:24:02,760
I never intended to be your burden either.

456
00:24:03,660 --> 00:24:04,880
You didn't even say "thank you."

457
00:24:04,970 --> 00:24:07,520
I will thank you all at once

458
00:24:07,570 --> 00:24:09,980
by returning the favor with total devastation.

459
00:24:10,180 --> 00:24:13,170
I will make sure
it is an experience to remember.

460
00:24:13,230 --> 00:24:14,280
Whoa.

461
00:24:15,950 --> 00:24:16,870
Stick to your word,

462
00:24:17,480 --> 00:24:18,360
Snoop.

463
00:24:18,920 --> 00:24:19,850
Come on, let's go.

464
00:24:23,090 --> 00:24:23,870
Hey...

465
00:24:23,910 --> 00:24:24,880
wait for me.

466
00:24:25,810 --> 00:24:26,880
Mr. Sarm!

467
00:24:27,970 --> 00:24:29,450
Mr. Sarm...

468
00:24:29,880 --> 00:24:30,600
This way!

469
00:24:41,410 --> 00:24:42,570
Mr. Sarm,

470
00:24:43,120 --> 00:24:45,520
you eat like a competitive eater.

471
00:24:45,880 --> 00:24:47,380
Just enjoy your crab fried rice

472
00:24:48,540 --> 00:24:49,780
and leave my food alone.

473
00:24:50,260 --> 00:24:51,800
Why so stingy?

474
00:24:53,100 --> 00:24:54,160
Take that back.

475
00:24:54,220 --> 00:24:55,120
I'm stingy?

476
00:24:55,200 --> 00:24:57,570
I ordered you this big platter
of crab fried rice.

477
00:24:57,990 --> 00:24:58,680
Eat up already.

478
00:24:58,880 --> 00:24:59,600
Whoa.

479
00:24:59,680 --> 00:25:01,890
You are eating three kilograms each

480
00:25:01,930 --> 00:25:03,270
of shellfish and crab.

481
00:25:03,980 --> 00:25:05,000
That is totally unfair.

482
00:25:05,160 --> 00:25:05,870
Hey.

483
00:25:05,970 --> 00:25:07,920
Be polite when talking to
your elders, alright?

484
00:25:07,990 --> 00:25:09,120
If you keep being this full of yourself,

485
00:25:09,220 --> 00:25:10,480
no one will share anything with you.

486
00:25:10,640 --> 00:25:11,920
You are full of excuses.

487
00:25:23,710 --> 00:25:24,660
You want some?

488
00:25:32,780 --> 00:25:33,780
Try closing your eyes.

489
00:25:34,450 --> 00:25:35,060
Closing my eyes?

490
00:25:35,100 --> 00:25:35,980
Do it.

491
00:25:37,980 --> 00:25:39,070
Close your eyes...

492
00:25:40,730 --> 00:25:41,580
and just dream about

493
00:25:41,630 --> 00:25:43,520
eating seafood.

494
00:25:43,770 --> 00:25:44,480
Are you full now?

495
00:25:44,520 --> 00:25:45,560
Gosh!

496
00:25:45,630 --> 00:25:47,440
You have endless money,

497
00:25:47,530 --> 00:25:50,120
yet you will not even spare me a few crabs?

498
00:25:52,840 --> 00:25:54,570
I don't waste my time on petty chatter.

499
00:25:54,720 --> 00:25:56,380
Can you

500
00:25:56,440 --> 00:25:57,390
even spell

501
00:25:57,420 --> 00:25:58,200
"generosity?"

502
00:25:58,230 --> 00:25:59,230
Uh...

503
00:25:59,260 --> 00:26:00,260
Mm...

504
00:26:00,300 --> 00:26:01,020
Oh.

505
00:26:02,090 --> 00:26:03,000
I don't.

506
00:26:16,480 --> 00:26:17,480
You want some?

507
00:26:19,360 --> 00:26:19,960
Ask nicely.

508
00:26:20,000 --> 00:26:20,960
I would rather not.

509
00:26:22,430 --> 00:26:25,910
I will remember how stingy you are.

510
00:26:26,520 --> 00:26:28,520
I will make sure I never forget it.

511
00:26:43,170 --> 00:26:43,850
Here.

512
00:26:49,560 --> 00:26:50,290
Take it.

513
00:26:50,590 --> 00:26:51,590
Mr. Sarm,

514
00:26:52,960 --> 00:26:54,880
you are always
blowing hot and cold with me.

515
00:26:55,920 --> 00:26:57,160
Just so you know,

516
00:26:57,580 --> 00:26:59,000
once you regain your strength,

517
00:26:59,030 --> 00:27:01,660
you'll go back to constantly shouting at me.

518
00:27:01,890 --> 00:27:02,680
You know that?

519
00:27:08,840 --> 00:27:09,370
You can't have that.

520
00:27:09,400 --> 00:27:10,240
Hey, you...

521
00:27:10,360 --> 00:27:11,280
Do not play with your food.

522
00:27:11,320 --> 00:27:12,260
"Do not play with your food."

523
00:27:12,280 --> 00:27:12,990
Play what?

524
00:27:14,410 --> 00:27:15,080
Give it back.

525
00:27:15,190 --> 00:27:15,700
Hey!

526
00:27:15,730 --> 00:27:16,380
You know,

527
00:27:16,450 --> 00:27:18,270
crabs have families, too.

528
00:27:18,310 --> 00:27:19,960
This is a crab family with their baby.

529
00:27:20,000 --> 00:27:21,000
You can't tear them apart.

530
00:27:21,680 --> 00:27:22,600
Eat that instead.

531
00:27:22,690 --> 00:27:24,470
They're a family. How dare you separate them?

532
00:27:24,680 --> 00:27:25,150
Gosh.

533
00:27:28,590 --> 00:27:30,000
No one can hurt you.

534
00:27:30,190 --> 00:27:31,000
Don't worry.

535
00:27:33,580 --> 00:27:34,640
Oh, I'm sorry.

536
00:27:35,760 --> 00:27:37,150
[Restaurant]

537
00:27:37,190 --> 00:27:38,520
[Flora Aloha]
[Reception, 100 meters]

538
00:27:51,510 --> 00:27:52,190
Give me your hand.

539
00:27:56,580 --> 00:27:57,780
You're such a burden.

540
00:27:57,840 --> 00:27:58,840
You were the one

541
00:27:58,890 --> 00:28:00,280
who dragged me onto the boat.

542
00:28:17,240 --> 00:28:17,870
Good evening.

543
00:28:17,910 --> 00:28:19,200
Good evening.

544
00:28:19,380 --> 00:28:21,290
Could I borrow the phone for a moment?

545
00:28:22,080 --> 00:28:22,890
Uh...

546
00:28:23,030 --> 00:28:24,360
We're really sorry.

547
00:28:24,390 --> 00:28:25,580
There's a storm right now.

548
00:28:25,620 --> 00:28:28,080
The phone signal and Internet are down.

549
00:28:29,290 --> 00:28:31,380
They're expected to be back
in about three days.

550
00:28:31,680 --> 00:28:33,050
We apologize for the inconvenience.

551
00:28:33,580 --> 00:28:34,580
Thank you.

552
00:29:56,790 --> 00:29:57,200
Huh?

553
00:29:59,510 --> 00:30:00,280
What?

554
00:30:00,690 --> 00:30:01,980
What are you doing here?

555
00:30:02,640 --> 00:30:05,080
You rented this resort for me, did you not?

556
00:30:08,410 --> 00:30:09,360
What are you on about?

557
00:30:10,200 --> 00:30:11,170
You...

558
00:30:11,470 --> 00:30:12,470
You are staying here, too?

559
00:30:15,690 --> 00:30:17,640
You think you have that much of a choice?

560
00:30:17,750 --> 00:30:18,750
But...

561
00:30:20,450 --> 00:30:21,250
Your room

562
00:30:21,290 --> 00:30:22,360
is this way.

563
00:31:16,880 --> 00:31:18,090
Knock, knock, knock.

564
00:31:56,370 --> 00:31:57,340
Do it!

565
00:31:58,970 --> 00:32:01,080
There are security cameras all over the beach.

566
00:32:01,770 --> 00:32:03,680
Your names will be known across the island.

567
00:32:24,680 --> 00:32:26,400
Mr. Sarm...

568
00:32:28,760 --> 00:32:29,960
Mr. Sarm...

569
00:32:36,680 --> 00:32:37,720
You want some?

570
00:32:44,880 --> 00:32:46,770
You're pretty cute when you're quiet,

571
00:32:49,080 --> 00:32:50,160
you spooky kitten.

572
00:32:57,130 --> 00:32:57,680
Hey.

573
00:33:12,710 --> 00:33:13,370
Hey, you.

574
00:33:26,920 --> 00:33:28,300
- Mm.
- Oh...

575
00:33:28,970 --> 00:33:31,390
Oh, my!

576
00:33:31,680 --> 00:33:32,680
What is it?

577
00:33:35,790 --> 00:33:36,600
Hey.

578
00:33:36,710 --> 00:33:38,080
You're not going to take a shower?

579
00:33:38,110 --> 00:33:40,040
Gosh, we've been to so many places today.

580
00:33:40,070 --> 00:33:42,270
We've been out in the sea breeze,
the sun, and the rain all day.

581
00:33:42,320 --> 00:33:44,200
What if you get sick and die?

582
00:33:45,690 --> 00:33:46,510
If you die,

583
00:33:46,570 --> 00:33:48,100
I'll let the stingrays have you.

584
00:33:50,300 --> 00:33:51,680
I'm not worried about you or anything.

585
00:33:57,590 --> 00:33:59,600
What are you doing in my bedroom anyway?

586
00:34:01,390 --> 00:34:02,480
Hey, I've been sitting here

587
00:34:02,510 --> 00:34:03,510
for over five minutes

588
00:34:03,550 --> 00:34:04,350
just to see

589
00:34:04,380 --> 00:34:05,600
if you've showered yet.

590
00:34:06,880 --> 00:34:08,270
You didn't even care...

591
00:34:10,639 --> 00:34:12,080
and you still refuse to take a shower.

592
00:34:12,150 --> 00:34:13,280
With the A/C this cold,

593
00:34:13,320 --> 00:34:15,190
what if you get sick and die?

594
00:34:18,699 --> 00:34:20,300
You are the one who has to go.

595
00:34:20,850 --> 00:34:22,040
This is my bedroom, after all.

596
00:34:23,620 --> 00:34:24,850
Go take a shower already.

597
00:34:25,520 --> 00:34:26,199
Here.

598
00:34:26,389 --> 00:34:26,920
Huh?

599
00:34:26,989 --> 00:34:27,800
I'll take you to the bathroom.

600
00:34:27,960 --> 00:34:28,440
Huh?

601
00:34:28,489 --> 00:34:29,980
Come on. I'll take you to shower.

602
00:34:30,020 --> 00:34:31,469
I'll shower after you, Jam.

603
00:34:33,100 --> 00:34:34,560
You go first.

604
00:34:34,659 --> 00:34:35,719
This is my bedroom.

605
00:34:36,300 --> 00:34:37,139
Fine.

606
00:34:37,179 --> 00:34:38,170
I guess I'll leave.

607
00:34:42,550 --> 00:34:43,820
Mr. Sarm...

608
00:34:44,010 --> 00:34:47,179
He cannot stop saying unpleasant things.

609
00:35:22,880 --> 00:35:23,640
Hey, mister.

610
00:35:23,680 --> 00:35:25,360
Do you think I'm high up in the tree?

611
00:35:35,800 --> 00:35:37,090
I thought I could finally rest.

612
00:35:39,240 --> 00:35:40,790
Then something came up again.

613
00:35:41,580 --> 00:35:42,140
Huh.

614
00:35:42,180 --> 00:35:43,760
You can't climb a tree, can you?

615
00:35:49,280 --> 00:35:50,370
I can't, obviously.

616
00:35:50,970 --> 00:35:51,970
But I'll tell you this:

617
00:35:52,260 --> 00:35:53,480
I won't lose to anyone.

618
00:35:54,490 --> 00:35:55,740
You call that high?

619
00:35:57,270 --> 00:35:57,800
Watch this.

620
00:36:16,620 --> 00:36:17,180
Ah!

621
00:36:35,380 --> 00:36:37,980
Jam, come and look at this.

622
00:36:40,080 --> 00:36:40,960
Mr. Sarm?

623
00:36:42,880 --> 00:36:43,880
No need to scream;

624
00:36:43,910 --> 00:36:44,980
I do daring things like this every day.

625
00:36:45,640 --> 00:36:47,000
What on earth are you doing up there?

626
00:36:47,060 --> 00:36:48,120
The kids challenged me.

627
00:36:48,390 --> 00:36:49,470
It is true that they did,

628
00:36:49,750 --> 00:36:51,680
but you did not have to act tough
and take the challenge.

629
00:36:51,800 --> 00:36:54,520
Can you even spell "give in"?

630
00:36:54,690 --> 00:36:56,360
Pull yourself together.

631
00:36:56,390 --> 00:36:57,360
Quit rambling, will you?

632
00:36:57,540 --> 00:36:58,480
Help me down first.

633
00:36:58,680 --> 00:36:59,600
Cannot be bothered.

634
00:36:59,780 --> 00:37:01,500
You got yourself up there,
so get yourself down.

635
00:37:02,680 --> 00:37:03,470
Let's go.

636
00:37:04,680 --> 00:37:05,320
Jam.

637
00:37:07,760 --> 00:37:08,760
Ow...

638
00:37:45,470 --> 00:37:46,700
Did it hurt that much?

639
00:37:46,840 --> 00:37:48,070
Oh, these scratches?

640
00:37:48,110 --> 00:37:48,840
Nothing at all.

641
00:37:48,880 --> 00:37:49,750
Nowhere near my heart.

642
00:37:55,500 --> 00:37:56,500
Ow.

643
00:38:05,020 --> 00:38:06,440
I will be gentle, okay?

644
00:38:08,280 --> 00:38:09,360
Let me know if it hurts.

645
00:38:09,960 --> 00:38:10,920
Okay.

646
00:38:18,560 --> 00:38:20,310
Ouch, ouch, ouch.

647
00:38:20,700 --> 00:38:21,490
Jam!

648
00:38:21,720 --> 00:38:22,760
Are you trying to murder me?!

649
00:38:23,520 --> 00:38:24,800
You're still laughing?!

650
00:38:26,410 --> 00:38:27,520
Ow...

651
00:38:30,490 --> 00:38:31,490
Want me to patch you up?

652
00:38:43,420 --> 00:38:44,280
Listen.

653
00:38:45,300 --> 00:38:47,090
Do not do crazy stunts again.

654
00:38:48,830 --> 00:38:49,770
Crazy stunts?

655
00:38:54,550 --> 00:38:56,370
Ever since I met you,

656
00:38:57,280 --> 00:38:59,280
you have been nothing but trouble.

657
00:39:03,920 --> 00:39:04,690
What did I do?

658
00:39:07,550 --> 00:39:08,870
When I first met you,

659
00:39:08,910 --> 00:39:10,040
you were drunk and causing a scene.

660
00:39:10,800 --> 00:39:11,880
After that,

661
00:39:11,910 --> 00:39:13,220
you jumped into the water on your own.

662
00:39:14,810 --> 00:39:15,720
Today,

663
00:39:15,770 --> 00:39:17,440
you had a tree-climbing contest
with the kids.

664
00:39:18,760 --> 00:39:20,470
And now you have gotten yourself hurt.

665
00:39:21,840 --> 00:39:23,300
I still do not know
what you have been doing

666
00:39:23,330 --> 00:39:25,040
for the past six months.

667
00:39:25,090 --> 00:39:26,970
But from what I can tell,

668
00:39:28,370 --> 00:39:30,430
you probably do not live
like normal people do, right?

669
00:39:30,480 --> 00:39:31,600
You're good at guessing.

670
00:39:32,380 --> 00:39:33,640
Can you tell me

671
00:39:34,240 --> 00:39:35,520
what you have been doing?

672
00:39:37,360 --> 00:39:39,080
I want to know

673
00:39:39,270 --> 00:39:41,180
what kind of cool things

674
00:39:42,070 --> 00:39:43,920
a cool guy like you likes to do.

675
00:39:46,070 --> 00:39:46,960
Finally,

676
00:39:47,360 --> 00:39:48,360
something nice to hear.

677
00:39:48,390 --> 00:39:50,970
You did not go out, capsize a boat,
and end up floating

678
00:39:51,000 --> 00:39:52,120
in the ocean at night, did you?

679
00:39:52,290 --> 00:39:54,580
That helps put my mind at ease, though.

680
00:39:55,620 --> 00:39:56,720
But it is dangerous.

681
00:39:56,870 --> 00:39:58,600
At night, the land breeze blows out to sea.

682
00:39:58,730 --> 00:40:00,840
You might vanish with the tide
before you know it.

683
00:40:00,920 --> 00:40:03,120
It's normal to feel like
doing something daring, right?

684
00:40:03,770 --> 00:40:06,380
Still feel like doing that now?

685
00:40:06,930 --> 00:40:08,240
I do not think so.

686
00:40:09,610 --> 00:40:10,480
Don't lay it on so thick.

687
00:40:10,520 --> 00:40:11,670
I already feel guilty enough.

688
00:40:14,050 --> 00:40:14,920
Oh, you.

689
00:40:17,100 --> 00:40:19,060
24 hours on this island

690
00:40:19,090 --> 00:40:21,560
feel like 24 years to me.

691
00:40:21,750 --> 00:40:24,160
There's the mystery behind
why people are hunting Mr. Sarm,

692
00:40:24,320 --> 00:40:26,610
why he refuses to go home,

693
00:40:26,850 --> 00:40:29,760
and how to mend his heart.

694
00:40:29,820 --> 00:40:30,800
Gosh...

695
00:40:30,840 --> 00:40:33,000
I can't figure out any of them.

696
00:40:33,480 --> 00:40:34,320
Hey.

697
00:40:34,570 --> 00:40:35,300
Huh?

698
00:40:36,460 --> 00:40:37,630
Come and have a meal with me.

699
00:40:40,580 --> 00:40:42,080
You are inviting me?

700
00:40:42,800 --> 00:40:43,600
Yeah.

701
00:40:45,140 --> 00:40:46,390
Eating alone...

702
00:40:47,450 --> 00:40:49,000
makes everything taste a bit bland.

703
00:40:55,580 --> 00:40:56,190
Mm.

704
00:41:00,720 --> 00:41:02,020
- Why did you flinch?
- Ow!

705
00:41:02,040 --> 00:41:02,950
It hurts.

706
00:41:19,380 --> 00:41:22,270
Why do you refuse to go back
to your bungalow to pack your things?

707
00:41:23,090 --> 00:41:25,800
You left a lot of your things back there.

708
00:41:26,920 --> 00:41:27,860
There's so much stuff.

709
00:41:28,280 --> 00:41:29,080
It's such a hassle

710
00:41:29,160 --> 00:41:30,520
to move it all.

711
00:41:30,780 --> 00:41:32,400
Still, there are
so many of your things there.

712
00:41:32,720 --> 00:41:34,490
If someone found out,

713
00:41:34,590 --> 00:41:35,690
it could get you into trouble.

714
00:41:35,720 --> 00:41:37,080
Are you worried about me or my stuff?

715
00:41:37,650 --> 00:41:38,850
I am...

716
00:41:40,480 --> 00:41:41,480
worried about my work.

717
00:41:41,610 --> 00:41:42,310
Huh...

718
00:41:43,420 --> 00:41:44,290
Worried about your work?

719
00:41:45,040 --> 00:41:46,410
Have you been back in Thailand long?

720
00:41:46,490 --> 00:41:48,200
I came back here when I was seven

721
00:41:48,880 --> 00:41:50,690
and have been living here ever since.

722
00:41:51,120 --> 00:41:51,990
Have you thought about...

723
00:41:52,460 --> 00:41:54,840
when you'll leave for a place
where you'll find peace?

724
00:41:55,000 --> 00:41:58,560
I will find peace after you kick the bucket.

725
00:42:01,060 --> 00:42:02,720
Sharp tongue, aren't you?

726
00:42:03,760 --> 00:42:04,640
How old are you?

727
00:42:05,820 --> 00:42:06,480
23?

728
00:42:06,580 --> 00:42:08,000
Why do you care?

729
00:42:08,500 --> 00:42:09,980
Age is just a number.

730
00:42:10,240 --> 00:42:10,750
Hey.

731
00:42:11,200 --> 00:42:12,600
Where did Sib find you, anyway?

732
00:42:13,040 --> 00:42:13,840
I mean...

733
00:42:14,670 --> 00:42:16,080
how did you end up working with him?

734
00:42:17,460 --> 00:42:18,760
If I answer your question,

735
00:42:18,870 --> 00:42:20,600
you have to answer mine, too.

736
00:42:20,650 --> 00:42:21,320
Wow...

737
00:42:21,400 --> 00:42:23,200
You really know
how to drive a hard bargain.

738
00:42:23,320 --> 00:42:24,200
But that's okay.

739
00:42:24,440 --> 00:42:25,320
I'm always fair.

740
00:42:25,340 --> 00:42:26,370
You ask, I ask.

741
00:42:26,740 --> 00:42:27,650
You answer, I answer.

742
00:42:28,650 --> 00:42:30,080
Why did you come to Ko Pha-ngan?

743
00:42:30,170 --> 00:42:30,920
I was heartbroken.

744
00:42:31,020 --> 00:42:31,800
My turn.

745
00:42:31,850 --> 00:42:34,480
You were sent to find
a good-looking guy like me.

746
00:42:34,680 --> 00:42:35,600
Isn't your partner jealous?

747
00:42:36,030 --> 00:42:37,240
My partner understands that

748
00:42:37,290 --> 00:42:38,480
I am here for work.

749
00:42:38,610 --> 00:42:39,920
A fictional partner doesn't count.

750
00:42:40,910 --> 00:42:42,120
So what?

751
00:42:43,100 --> 00:42:44,960
My turn, then.

752
00:42:46,080 --> 00:42:47,700
Now that you have abandoned your work,

753
00:42:48,460 --> 00:42:49,880
who has taken the helm?

754
00:42:50,000 --> 00:42:50,720
Thee, obviously.

755
00:42:51,110 --> 00:42:52,080
I'm close to him.

756
00:42:53,920 --> 00:42:55,600
I might even be closer to him
than I am to Sib.

757
00:42:55,700 --> 00:42:56,960
Oh.

758
00:42:57,130 --> 00:42:58,360
Like what Song said.

759
00:42:58,800 --> 00:43:00,120
Mr. Thee...

760
00:43:00,200 --> 00:43:02,780
Is he a relative of yours
around the same age as Mr. Sib?

761
00:43:02,840 --> 00:43:03,840
You call him by his name?

762
00:43:04,480 --> 00:43:05,320
Are you two close?

763
00:43:05,430 --> 00:43:07,080
That is what Dr. Song wants me to call him.

764
00:43:07,280 --> 00:43:08,240
I'm the same age as Song,

765
00:43:08,280 --> 00:43:09,400
and I'm way older than you.

766
00:43:09,440 --> 00:43:10,410
Why don't you call me the same way?

767
00:43:10,440 --> 00:43:12,680
Why do you not
address me more politely, then?

768
00:43:16,560 --> 00:43:17,880
My turn.

769
00:43:19,590 --> 00:43:21,270
When are you returning home?

770
00:43:22,730 --> 00:43:23,870
Probably not anytime soon.

771
00:43:25,210 --> 00:43:26,490
Wanna sing a song?

772
00:43:26,560 --> 00:43:28,190
Get a perfect 100,

773
00:43:28,220 --> 00:43:29,580
and your food is on the house.

774
00:43:30,650 --> 00:43:31,510
No, thank you.

775
00:43:31,960 --> 00:43:32,880
What a shame.

776
00:43:32,920 --> 00:43:35,260
Someone got a perfect score this afternoon,

777
00:43:35,290 --> 00:43:36,780
so their bill was on us.

778
00:43:37,400 --> 00:43:38,070
Where's the microphone?

779
00:43:41,410 --> 00:43:42,580
You scared me.

780
00:43:43,890 --> 00:43:45,280
I'm Four, and you're Mod.

781
00:43:45,320 --> 00:43:46,760
Hey, wait...

782
00:43:46,860 --> 00:43:47,310
What?

783
00:43:47,350 --> 00:43:48,350
Please no.

784
00:43:48,490 --> 00:43:49,200
I am embarrassed.

785
00:43:49,240 --> 00:43:50,030
Oh, embarrassed about what?

786
00:43:50,050 --> 00:43:50,920
There are so many people here.

787
00:43:51,730 --> 00:43:53,210
That is what makes it

788
00:43:53,240 --> 00:43:54,480
even more embarrassing!

789
00:43:54,560 --> 00:43:55,560
Oh, don't feel that way.

790
00:43:55,700 --> 00:43:56,560
Come on, let's go.

791
00:43:56,740 --> 00:43:57,840
Sing a song!

792
00:44:00,220 --> 00:44:01,580
We've found Mr. Sarm.

793
00:44:01,620 --> 00:44:03,280
He's on the fishing village side
of the island

794
00:44:03,370 --> 00:44:04,790
with Mr. Sattawat's assistant.

795
00:44:04,820 --> 00:44:05,480
Let's do this.

796
00:44:05,510 --> 00:44:06,610
Alright.

797
00:44:06,640 --> 00:44:07,970
Leave the assistant be.

798
00:44:08,010 --> 00:44:09,120
I want no trouble with him.

799
00:44:09,150 --> 00:44:10,060
As for Sarm,

800
00:44:10,100 --> 00:44:11,930
if disappearing is truly what he wants,

801
00:44:11,990 --> 00:44:14,400
let us grant him his wish.

802
00:44:14,570 --> 00:44:15,570
Understood.

803
00:44:24,470 --> 00:44:28,160
[Mission: Hunt Down the Teeny-tiny Tiger]

804
00:44:28,590 --> 00:44:30,460
My mission

805
00:44:30,510 --> 00:44:31,760
is not yet complete.

806
00:44:31,790 --> 00:44:33,890
Mr. Sarm still refuses to return home.

807
00:44:34,090 --> 00:44:35,930
However, today,

808
00:44:36,020 --> 00:44:37,900
I came to understand that

809
00:44:37,930 --> 00:44:39,590
it is not his body

810
00:44:39,690 --> 00:44:41,680
trying to escape,

811
00:44:41,800 --> 00:44:44,000
but his heart seeking refuge.

812
00:44:44,310 --> 00:44:47,040
Over the past 24 hours,

813
00:44:47,110 --> 00:44:49,830
I have seen a man
who pretends to be tough,

814
00:44:49,920 --> 00:44:51,730
fights against his own feelings,

815
00:44:51,760 --> 00:44:53,710
loves to win,

816
00:44:54,000 --> 00:44:56,720
and refuses to let anyone know
when he is in pain.

817
00:44:57,890 --> 00:44:59,290
Maybe...

818
00:44:59,680 --> 00:45:01,730
bringing him home

819
00:45:01,950 --> 00:45:04,460
is not about bringing him back to the farm,

820
00:45:04,490 --> 00:45:05,630
but about...

821
00:45:05,650 --> 00:45:08,480
bringing him back to his old self.

822
00:45:08,560 --> 00:45:10,040
And it seems like...

823
00:45:10,490 --> 00:45:13,380
my mission has only just begun.

824
00:45:13,950 --> 00:45:15,590
If you want to get over it,

825
00:45:15,640 --> 00:45:17,520
the first step is accepting the truth.

826
00:45:20,000 --> 00:45:21,330
Someday,

827
00:45:21,430 --> 00:45:23,330
you will find someone you love

828
00:45:23,440 --> 00:45:24,630
who loves you back.

829
00:45:27,930 --> 00:45:30,130
We've been through so much together,

830
00:45:32,200 --> 00:45:33,410
so how about we become friends?

831
00:45:34,840 --> 00:45:35,840
Mr. Sarm!

832
00:45:36,160 --> 00:45:37,310
Where are you, Mr. Sarm?

833
00:45:40,370 --> 00:45:45,040
♫I'm here to love you as myself,
not as a surrogate♫

834
00:45:45,070 --> 00:45:48,820
♫Let me be your safe space
when you need a break♫

835
00:45:48,850 --> 00:45:53,840
♫Who cares if I'm not your first or second?♫

836
00:45:53,950 --> 00:45:58,720
♫At least being your third still counts♫

837
00:45:58,750 --> 00:46:03,340
♫I'm here to love you,
no matter who left you with heartache♫

838
00:46:03,390 --> 00:46:07,050
♫Just let me heal your heart,
lending you my aid♫

839
00:46:07,080 --> 00:46:12,190
♫Have faith and believe in love once more♫

840
00:46:12,220 --> 00:46:14,200
♫'Cause good love is your Lucky Third♫

841
00:46:14,230 --> 00:46:17,720
♫Your Third, can it be me, love?♫

842
00:46:30,540 --> 00:46:32,520
♫'Cause good love is your Lucky Third♫

843
00:46:32,550 --> 00:46:35,790
♫Your Third, can it be me, love?♫

844
00:46:37,110 --> 00:46:39,340
[Your Third Series]
